# The three-Oblivion-Ring loop again (CR 104.4b), but Bot2 holds Disenchant with two untapped Plains. The Rings are alike,
# so the game comes back to the same position each time a Ring leaves (two passes of Bot2's). A loop every player only
# passes in is let go round before the game is a draw (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-4), so that a player holding an answer
# outside it may still end it. Bot2 passes twelve times, and the game goes on; then it breaks the loop, at its last
# priority before the draw. After the twelfth pass, as after the sixth, Ring A has just been exiled with Ring B and A's
# leaves ability (which will return C) is on the stack, B alone on the battlefield; Disenchant destroys B. B's leaves
# ability returns A, whose enters ability has no other nonland permanent to target and is removed (CR 603.3d); then the
# old A's leaves ability returns C, whose enters ability exiles A, whose leaves ability returns nothing (it is a new A, CR
# 400.7, that exiled nothing). One Ring is left on the battlefield holding one in exile, and the game goes on.

[Bot1 Deck]
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Disenchant
Island x20

